//? Title: SARSA: actual behavior actions, on-policy targets and cliff returns
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Learn action values from sampled state-action-reward-state-action transitions.
Native action and update histories expose the on-policy bootstrap; the original
4-by-12 cliff experiment compares SARSA and Q-learning using the same controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For a nonterminal transition, sample the next epsilon-greedy behavior action
before updating:
$$ Q(s,a)\leftarrow Q(s,a)+\alpha\{r+\gamma Q(s',a')-Q(s,a)\}. $$
\alttext(SARSA updates the current action value toward reward plus the discounted next sampled behavior action value.)
Terminal transitions use zero bootstrap. Q-learning instead uses the maximum
next-state action value. Constant exploration makes cliff risk part of the
behavior return. The original finite constant-rate, single-seed experiment
illustrates this distinction without proving optimality or comparing
statistically independent populations. Initial action selection occurs even with
a zero-step episode; every nonterminal transition selects a next action,
including the final capped transition.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sarsa_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/sarsa.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::RLParameters p;
    p.episodes = 1;
    p.max_steps = 4;
    p.seed = 7;
    auto r = a::sarsa_trace(a::tabular_corridor(3), p);
    std::print("| actual state | actual action | reward | next state | terminal | bootstrap | target | " "after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.state,
                   s.action, s.reward, s.next_state, s.terminal, s.bootstrap,
                   s.target, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Sample actual behavior action");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual sampled transitions {}",
                                     r.transitions));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual selections {}", r.action_selections));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sarsa_tiny.svg");
}
```
