> Actual selected work and sensitivity

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sarsa_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/sarsa.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| epsilon | actual transitions | exploratory selections | final trailing-50 reward |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (double epsilon : {0.0, .05, .1, .2, .4}) {
        a::RLParameters p;
        p.learning_rate = .5;
        p.discount = 1;
        p.epsilon = epsilon;
        p.episodes = 500;
        p.max_steps = 2000;
        p.seed = 7;
        auto r = a::sarsa_run(a::tabular_cliff(), p);
        auto mean =
            a::trailing_return_mean(r.result.episode_returns, 50).back();
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", epsilon, r.transitions,
                   r.exploratory_actions, mean);
        x.push_back(epsilon);
        y.push_back(mean);
    }
    auto plot = g::RPlot::create();
    plot.lines(x, y, "actual values", {37, 99, 235}).points(x, y, {37, 99, 235},
                                                            5).title(
        "Single-seed behavior sensitivity to exploration").x_label("epsilon").y_label("actual last-50 mean reward");
    plot.save_svg("build/sarsa_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| epsilon | actual transitions | exploratory selections | final trailing-50 reward |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 8393 | 0 | -13 |
| 0.05 | 11265 | 548 | -20.36 |
| 0.1 | 13536 | 1291 | -23.84 |
| 0.2 | 14518 | 2880 | -41.22 |
| 0.4 | 27701 | 11081 | -77.68 |
\image(figures/sarsa_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual selected event counts or represented numerical outcomes; raw values are retained in the computed table.)
\alttext(Actual selected event counts or represented numerical outcomes; raw values are retained in the computed table.)

> API and interpretation

All geometry, controls and returned state IDs/rewards are checked before
indexing, including terminal states. Actual selections include
selected-but-unused final next actions. Training returns and greedy evaluation
are different quantities. Callback side effects cannot be rolled back. Epsilon
sensitivity uses a fixed seed and does not claim statistical significance.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Sutton and Barto, Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction, second edition, chapter 6|https://incompleteideas.net/book/the-book-2nd.html]

Verification: all four complete programs executed; all four figures were
rendered and visually reviewed. HTML and Markdown exports preserve every
computed table and image. This ten-topic batch passes 89 scoped native cases, 21
directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 95 executable public examples, 469/469
scoped documentation definitions, ten representative editor hovers and 3677
independent oracle records with 28988 checks. Frozen compatibility checks record
the intentional final-posterior RVM change. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-334-343/`.
